{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966797,"nonce":"t7MOmEx9fG7CzbpAX1aU/jp1IdU=","title":"Calling OverlayHandle::is_live() / is_exiting() / close() inside a held","message":"`OverlayHandle::is_live()`, `is_exiting()`, and `close()` are sugar that\ninternally call `overlay_stack().lock()` to inspect or mutate the stack.\n\nIf you call any of them inside a scope where you already hold\n`overlay_stack().lock()`, you re-enter the same `std::sync::Mutex` from\nthe same thread. On std this either deadlocks (most platforms) or\npanics with \"lock poisoned\" (some). User-visible symptom: the app hangs\nafter a hover / click that triggers the path.\n\n\nUser report: \"Two hover cards showed at the same time then it hangs.\"\n\nThe card content's `on_hover_enter` did:\n\n```rust\n.on_hover_enter(move |_| {\n    if let Ok(mut stack) = overlay_stack().lock() {\n        if handle.is_exiting() {           // ← re-enters mutex → deadlock\n            stack.revive(handle);\n        } else {\n            stack.handle_mouse_enter(handle);\n        }\n    }\n})\n```\n\nMouse moved over the card → handler fired → outer lock acquired →\n`is_exiting()` tried to acquire the same lock → block forever.\n\n\n**Inside a held `overlay_stack().lock()` scope**, never call:\n- `OverlayHandle::is_live()`\n- `OverlayHandle::is_exiting()`\n- `OverlayHandle::close()`\n- Any other method that calls `overlay_stack().lock()` under the hood\n\nInstead, inspect the `MutexGuard` directly:\n\n```rust\nif let Ok(mut stack) = overlay_stack().lock() {\n    let exiting = stack\n        .iter_bottom_up()\n        .any(|e| e.handle == handle \u0026\u0026 e.exiting);\n    if exiting {\n        stack.revive(handle);\n    } else {\n        stack.handle_mouse_enter(handle);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Outside any held lock**, the sugar is fine and preferred:\n\n```rust\n// Trigger's on_hover_enter — no lock held yet.\nif handle.is_live() {\n    if let Ok(mut stack) = overlay_stack().lock() {\n        stack.handle_mouse_enter(handle);\n    }\n    return;\n}\n```\n\n`is_live()` acquires + releases its lock, then the explicit `.lock()`\nacquires fresh. Not nested.\n\n\nUnlike Rust's `RefCell` (which catches re-entrancy at runtime with a\npanic) or Java's `synchronized` (which re-grants the same thread),\n`std::sync::Mutex` blocks if the same thread tries to acquire a held\nlock. This is by design — re-entrancy hides real lock-order bugs.\n\nThe fix is always: don't nest, restructure the call.\n\n\n`ToastHandle::dismiss()` also calls `toast_tray().lock()` internally.\nSame rule applies: don't call it inside a held `toast_tray().lock()`\nscope. Inspect entries directly through the guard.\n\nFixed in commit `467cf65e`.\n\n\n`OverlayStack::begin_exit` called `entry.fire_on_close(reason)` while the\ncaller held `overlay_stack().lock()`. Latent for as long as no overlay\nreported its own dismissal — the close BUTTON works because it fires\nfrom event dispatch, outside the lock.\n\nIt surfaced when `cn::drawer`/`sheet`/`dialog` were wired to clear their\nbound signal on every dismissal route. That write re-enters whatever\ndrives the overlay (`cn_dsl::modal::sync`), which locks the stack again.\nInstant hang, and it took two attempts to see: the first looked like a\n`sync` problem, and restructuring `sync` alone did not fix it.\n\n**Fixed** by queueing: `begin_exit` pushes into\n`pending_close_callbacks`, and `drain_close_callbacks()` runs them once\nthe guard is gone — after each programmatic close, and once per frame in\nthe windowed runner so backdrop / Escape report a frame later. Two\n`overlay_stack` tests pinned the synchronous contract and now drain via\n`take_pending_close_callbacks`.\n\n**The rule this generalises to:** a lock held across a callback is a\ndeadlock waiting for someone to write an interesting callback. The\nexisting note above says \"don't nest, restructure the call\" for\n`OverlayHandle` methods; the same applies to the stack invoking anything\nit does not own.\n\nFixed in `4f1bd078`.","files":null}]}